"""Outbound-webhooks tests — requires the `db`, `users`, and `worker` extras.

NO live infrastructure: the arq pool is an in-memory fake (no Redis) and every outbound HTTP
call is mocked with respx (no network). Proves the contract end to end — endpoint CRUD, that
``dispatch`` ENQUEUES one signed delivery per subscribed endpoint, that the worker task POSTs the
event with a correct HMAC-SHA256 signature and retries on failure, and that a dead queue is
swallowed so the triggering request still succeeds. Runs against the throwaway SQLite database
from `conftest.pytest_configure`.
"""

